## Interaction model (CDP pointer events, real layout)

A temporary out-of-repo helper drove Chrome for Testing 156 through CDP
(`Emulation.setDeviceMetricsOverride`, `Page.navigate`, `Runtime.evaluate` with real
`PointerEvent`/`KeyboardEvent` dispatch, `Page.captureScreenshot`, `Emulation.setEmulatedMedia`) and
was removed afterwards. Screenshots are scrolled so the demo surface is visible.

```sh
node /tmp/p030-cdp.mjs "http://127.0.0.1:4200/apps/web/preview/?v=P0-30" "reviews/evidence"
```

### 1:1 pointer tracking, no mid-drag commit

Docked notepad dragged twice (world coordinates):

```
start:  pointer (567.0, 135.8)  item (447.0,  91.0) 240 × 88.6
mid:    pointer (440.0, 184.8)  item (320.0, 140.0) 240 × 88.6   delta (-127, +49) = (-127, +49)
end:    pointer (540.0, 244.8)  item (420.0, 200.0) 240 × 88.6   delta (+100, +60) = (+100, +60)
```

The item follows the pointer exactly; only the canvas edge clamps it. Mid-drag checks:

- grouping: after both items are free, dragging the window over the notepad gives
  `zone.data-zone-visible=false`, both items still `detached`, slot order unchanged
  `[notepad, window]`, and the drop hint only on the notepad (`is-drop-target`); the zone was not
  created mid-drag.
- reorder: inside a grouped zone, dragging the notepad over the window gives both items `docked`,
  slot order unchanged `[notepad, window]`, hint on the window; no orientation/size change mid-drag.

### Release commits

```
release free (outside):   notepad released outside the zone -> status "Notepad detached — free on
                          the canvas.", notepad state detached, window still docked, zone visible
release over hidden zone: zone hidden with both items detached; dragging a free item to the hidden
                          zone's old centre and releasing -> zone stays hidden (data-zone-visible
                          false), both items still detached, status unchanged "Zone hidden — drag
                          the two items together to form a new zone."
grouping on release:      window dragged over the free notepad, released -> new grouped zone,
                          both items docked, status "Items grouped stacked into a new zone."
collapse:                 detaching both items from a grouped zone hides the zone again
                          (data-zone-visible=false, is-collapsed)
```

### Orientation from the placement

```
vertical drop:    dragged the window onto the notepad from below (offset +10, +60) -> requested
                  vertical; zone 274 × 275 at (412.4, 78.7), insideWorld true, toolbarOverlap 0,
                  status "Items grouped stacked into a new zone."
horizontal drop:  dragged the window onto the notepad from the right (offset +90, +5) -> requested
                  horizontal; zone 526 × 174 at (316.4, 110.7), insideWorld true, toolbarOverlap 0,
                  status "Items grouped side by side into a new zone."
reorder/swap:     in the horizontal zone drag the notepad past the window's midpoint -> zone stays
                  horizontal 526 × 174, slot order [window, notepad], status "Order changed inside
                  the zone."
orientation flip: drag the window above the notepad -> zone becomes vertical 274 × 275, slot order
                  [window, notepad]
back:             drag it to the right again -> horizontal 526 × 174, slot order [notepad, window]
```

The zone animates its resize, measured while switching vertical 274 × 275 → horizontal 526 × 174:

```
t (ms)   inline-size   block-size   orientation attribute
   15       274px         275px      horizontal
   32       274px         275px      horizontal
   49       375.1px       234.5px    horizontal
   65       444.7px       206.6px    horizontal
   82       485.3px       190.3px    horizontal
   99       507.2px       181.5px    horizontal
  115       518.3px       177.1px    horizontal
  315       526px         174px      horizontal
```

`inline-size`/`block-size` transition over `--motion-panel` (180 ms) with the spring-like ease while
the items settle to their new slots.

### Resize re-fit (P0-29 kept)

```
1440 x 900 (grouped): horizontal 526 x 174 at (316.4, 110.7), insideWorld true
390 x 844:            fallback vertical 274 x 275 at (82, 110.7), world 356 x 744, insideWorld true,
                      toolbarOverlap 0, both items clipped=false
back at 1440 x 900:   horizontal 526 x 174 at (82, 110.7), insideWorld true
```

The requested orientation is kept; a fit fallback is used temporarily and restored when the surface
is wide enough again. Card A/B are user-placed canvas objects and are only clamped on viewport
changes (P0-24 behaviour), so the A/B edge path changes with the viewport — zone actions themselves
never touch the edge (docked, grouped, reordered, reduced-motion and re-grouped states share the same
A/B path at a fixed 1440 × 900 viewport).

