## Notes

- Thresholds in the code: visual detach ramp 28 screen px, release margin 18 screen px (outside =
  free, inside/within the band = dock/reorder), grouping 25 % overlap of the smaller area or 48
  screen px centre distance, orientation dominance 1.2 (hysteresis band for diagonal drops), order
  hysteresis 8 screen px around the midpoint, zone padding 16 px / gap 12 px, motion 180 ms with the
  spring eases above, detach scale max 1.03.
- The hidden zone is inert on both drag and release paths (P0-29); the zone comes back through
  re-grouping or by docking during the exit. The zone resize/collapse animations use the existing
  motion tokens; transform/opacity drive the item motion, while the committed orientation change
  animates the zone's inline/block size.
- Zone actions never create, move or change the A/B edge: exactly one `.demo__edge` element and one
  path in every measured state; only viewport changes (which clamp the user-placed cards) change it.

## Round 2 (rework after the fail review)

**Blocker A4 — rendered locale masthead.** The HTML fallback was correct, but `en.json`/`de.json`
still carried the P0-29 lines, so `applyLocale` overwrote the rendered masthead. Fixed in both JSONs:
`masthead.lastChange` = P0-30 title (EN) / German translation (DE), `masthead.tasks` includes P0-30,
`masthead.lastChangeTime` = 2026-10-27 11:12. Verified on the rendered page in EN and DE (values above,
captured as `P0-30-masthead-en.png` / `P0-30-masthead-de.png`) and after switching back to EN.

**Minor 1 — distinct orientation status.** Added `demo.status.orientationChanged` (EN "Orientation
changed inside the zone.", DE "Ausrichtung in der Zone geändert.") and split the reorder commit:
a real slot swap announces "Order changed inside the zone.", an axis flip without a slot swap
announces "Orientation changed inside the zone." Measured: horizontal zone [notepad, window] →
dragging the notepad above the window gives vertical, order unchanged [notepad, window], status
"Orientation changed inside the zone."; a following drop past the window gives horizontal, order
[window, notepad], status "Order changed inside the zone."

**Minor 2 — visible-surface fit at high zoom.** A grouped zone is now clamped into the **visible**
surface rectangle (`visibleWorldBounds()`: the intersection of the scaled world and the demo
surface), not just the world layer. At 150 % zoom the stacked request does not fit below the toolbar
so it uses the side-by-side fallback like before, but the position is clamped to the visible area:
zone screen rect (188.3, 111.7) 526 × 174 in world coordinates, `insideSurface` true,
`toolbarOverlap` 0; before the fix the same zone sat at x = 108.4 and was partly outside the visible
surface. Captured as `P0-30-zoom-150.png`. Ordinary 100 %/390 px fits are unchanged (`insideSurface`
also true there).

No other screenshots changed: the horizontal/vertical/swapped/drop-hint/controls captures were taken
at 100 % zoom in a fixed 1440 × 900 viewport, where the visible surface equals the world and the
status strings for those flows are unchanged. The round-1 gate records are superseded by the round-2
records in the gates table above and will not be committed.
